WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:01.550
[SPARKS POPPING]

00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:05.920
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.440
NARRATOR: We can't all rub
shoulders with political greats

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.200
and movie stars, but for
the price of admission

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.670
to a wax attraction, anyone can
mingle with their wax replicas.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.220
These look-alikes aren't
much for conversation,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.580
but the likeness can be
startling, thanks to a process

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.290
honed over centuries.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.190
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.770
Famous faces come
to life in beeswax,

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:33.740
so it's almost like
seeing them in the flesh.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.450
But how do they do it?

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.670
It often starts with
a face-to-face meeting

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.770
with the subject,
during which they take

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.440
more than 200 measurements
of the face alone,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:43.730
and still more of the body.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.750
Drawing on those
measurements and using photos

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.080
and additional research, an
artist sculpts a clay body

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.940
onto a metal skeleton.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.880
This clay sculpture will
be used to make a mold.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.850
The head, of course,
receives special attention.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.240
They sculpt it in stages, and
this takes about six weeks.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.930
To check the symmetry
of the sculptured face,

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.740
the artist stretches a wire
from the temple to the chin.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.650
She measures it from
all angles and compares

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.870
the numbers to measurements
of the actual subject.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.550
Every single aspect
of the clay face

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.280
must mirror that of the
subject's precisely,

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.690
so if it's even slightly
off, she makes adjustments.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:31.100
Here, she redefines
the teeth a bit more,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.555
and then she tweaks
the hairline.

00:01:32.555 --> 00:01:35.726
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.740
They're now ready
for the next step,

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.780
the making of the head mold.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.480
The worker paints plaster
onto the sculpture

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.650
in 14 different sections.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.790
This multi-part mold can be
easily removed from the clay

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.575
head once the plaster dries.

00:01:51.575 --> 00:01:54.740
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.340
After the clay head
has been discarded,

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.965
they give the reassembled
mold a quick rinse.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.500
The wax artist turns the
plaster head mold upside down

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.020
and slots it into
the wax bench, so

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.990
named because it secures the
mold during the wax casting.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.580
They melt blocks
of Japanese beeswax

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.820
and funnel the liquid wax into
the neck of the plaster cast.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.170
They let it set for an hour,
just long enough for the wax

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.540
to solidify and
form a thick crust

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.030
around the inside of the cast.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:31.340
The artist removes
crust at the neck

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.290
and pours out the
rest of the wax,

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.410
leaving a hollow
wax face inside.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:39.770
They set it aside for another
hour to further solidify.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:43.070
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.410
The wax artist
removes a plaster mold

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.795
and comes face to face
with the wax creation.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.620
She examines it
thoroughly, confirming

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.110
that the detail from the
mold has been effectively

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.920
transferred to the wax and that
the wax face is a dead ringer

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.140
for the human subject.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:03.290
The team then casts
the wax figure's hands,

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.030
and an artist
matches the subject's

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.580
skin tone against a chart.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.370
She mixes paint and
dabs the brush in it.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.930
She then strikes her
brush with another one,

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.380
so the paint splatters
across the hand.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.870
She blots up the
paint to blend it in.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.540
This technique gives
the wax a speckled look

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.890
that mimics human pores.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.440
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.650
She paints on knuckles, veins,
and distinctive markings

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:29.480
to mimic those on
the subject's hands.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.890
She gives the nails a manicure
to make the hands look

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.660
identical to the subject's.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.320
In the hands of
a skilled artist,

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.555
these wax hands
have come to life.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:46.130
As a medical glass
eye spins, the artist

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:50.480
blots on a very wide pupil first
and then paints the periphery

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.965
to mimic the person's iris.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.750
Iris color and pattern are
unique to the individual,

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.120
and the artist replicates
those qualities

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.770
as closely as possible.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:04.011
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.300
She glues red silk threads
onto the whites of the eyes

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.160
to simulate broken
blood vessels.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.430
It's another touch of realism.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:16.734
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:22.490
They slot the eyes into
sockets in the wax head.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.300
Then, the wax figure is ready
for its hair, actual human

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.760
hair matched to the subject's.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.710
They pierce the wax
with a hot needle

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:33.200
to insert each
hair individually.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.260
The wax melts and
closes around the hair.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.230
This process can
take four weeks.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.870
They also plug in
brows and lashes

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.360
and then brush on
paint like makeup.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.830
With his face on, the wax
figure now looks true to life.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.580
Once completed, wax figures
get movie-star treatment.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.490
Their hair is washed
and styled regularly,

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:58.310
and their clothing is
routinely dry cleaned.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.460
After all, even wax
versions of famous people

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:02.870
have to keep up appearances.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:06.220
[MUSIC PLAYING]

